# Applies to every Docker build in this repo whose context is the repo root (e.g.
# packages/relayer/Dockerfile, built via `docker build -f packages/relayer/Dockerfile .` or via
# packages/relayer/docker-compose.yml's `context: ../..`). Two things about .dockerignore that are
# NOT true of .gitignore, both confirmed by directly testing (not assumed) — see the STEP 6 report:
#
#   1. Docker only honors a .dockerignore at the BUILD CONTEXT'S ROOT. A .dockerignore nested inside
#      packages/relayer/ does NOT apply when the build context is the repo root, even though that is
#      where the Dockerfile itself lives.
#   2. A bare pattern like `.env` does NOT match recursively the way .gitignore's does — it only
#      matches a file named exactly `.env` AT THE CONTEXT ROOT. Every pattern below that needs to
#      match at any depth (packages/relayer/.env, packages/anything-else/.env, etc.) is written with
#      an explicit `**/` prefix for exactly this reason.

**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.turbo
**/coverage
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Secrets: .env files are created right next to docker-compose.yml per README.md's instructions, and
# must never end up baked into an image layer. .env.example is the one exception (no real secrets).
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

**/.DS_Store
.git

# Rust / Soroban contract build artifacts — irrelevant to any Node.js package's Docker build and
# unnecessarily large to include in the build context.
contracts/router/target
contracts/router/test_snapshots
